{"id":"2409.11404","authors":[{"_id":"66ec74ca3f928a11d82ee1e9","user":{"_id":"631e04cde4b67f5168f9144b","avatarUrl":"/avatars/45456c492613523f86825fdfd8ddcf9b.svg","isPro":false,"fullname":"Basel Mousi","user":"BaselMousi","type":"user","name":"BaselMousi"},"name":"Basel Mousi","status":"claimed_verified","statusLastChangedAt":"2024-11-04T11:37:18.921Z","hidden":false},{"_id":"66ec74ca3f928a11d82ee1ea","name":"Nadir Durrani","hidden":false},{"_id":"66ec74ca3f928a11d82ee1eb","name":"Fatema Ahmad","hidden":false},{"_id":"66ec74ca3f928a11d82ee1ec","name":"Md. Arid Hasan","hidden":false},{"_id":"66ec74ca3f928a11d82ee1ed","name":"Maram Hasanain","hidden":false},{"_id":"66ec74ca3f928a11d82ee1ee","name":"Tameem Kabbani","hidden":false},{"_id":"66ec74ca3f928a11d82ee1ef","name":"Fahim Dalvi","hidden":false},{"_id":"66ec74ca3f928a11d82ee1f0","name":"Shammur Absar Chowdhury","hidden":false},{"_id":"66ec74ca3f928a11d82ee1f1","user":{"_id":"60645d97b8b54bdb5a2d152b","avatarUrl":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/60645d97b8b54bdb5a2d152b/pCZ8s09kvJf9DkJfQbTpf.jpeg","isPro":false,"fullname":"Alam","user":"Firoj","type":"user","name":"Firoj"},"name":"Firoj Alam","status":"claimed_verified","statusLastChangedAt":"2026-02-11T11:23:52.481Z","hidden":false}],"publishedAt":"2024-09-17T17:59:25.000Z","title":"AraDiCE: Benchmarks for Dialectal and Cultural Capabilities in LLMs","summary":"Arabic, with its rich diversity of dialects, remains significantly\nunderrepresented in Large Language Models, particularly in dialectal\nvariations. We address this gap by introducing seven synthetic datasets in\ndialects alongside Modern Standard Arabic (MSA), created using Machine\nTranslation (MT) combined with human post-editing. We present AraDiCE, a\nbenchmark for Arabic Dialect and Cultural Evaluation. We evaluate LLMs on\ndialect comprehension and generation, focusing specifically on low-resource\nArabic dialects. Additionally, we introduce the first-ever fine-grained\nbenchmark designed to evaluate cultural awareness across the Gulf, Egypt, and\nLevant regions, providing a novel dimension to LLM evaluation. Our findings\ndemonstrate that while Arabic-specific models like Jais and AceGPT outperform\nmultilingual models on dialectal tasks, significant challenges persist in\ndialect identification, generation, and translation. This work contributes ~45K\npost-edited samples, a cultural benchmark, and highlights the importance of\ntailored training to improve LLM performance in capturing the nuances of\ndiverse Arabic dialects and cultural contexts. We will release the dialectal\ntranslation models and benchmarks curated in this study.","upvotes":0,"discussionId":"66ec74cb3f928a11d82ee22e","ai_summary":"The study introduces synthetic datasets and a benchmark to evaluate Large Language Models on Arabic dialect comprehension and generation, highlighting challenges and the importance of tailored training for dialectal and cultural diversity.","ai_keywords":["Synthetic datasets","Machine Translation","human post-editing","AraDiCE","benchmark","dialect comprehension","dialect generation","low-resource dialects","cultural awareness","Jais","AceGPT","dialect identification","dialect translation"],"ai_summary_model":"Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct","linkedModels":[{"author":"QCRI","authorData":{"_id":"5fbffdf6b9e35d457aa46bf6","avatarUrl":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6267a11207a1d53497266f64/ePblm2zgP_6jKtXbmitLJ.png","fullname":"Qatar Computing Research Institute","name":"QCRI","type":"org","isHf":false,"isHfAdmin":false,"isMod":false,"followerCount":182,"isUserFollowing":false},"downloads":17,"gated":false,"id":"QCRI/AraDiCE-msa-to-egy","availableInferenceProviders":[],"lastModified":"2024-12-09T15:55:48.000Z","likes":1,"pipeline_tag":"translation","private":false,"repoType":"model","isLikedByUser":false,"widgetOutputUrls":[],"numParameters":3344863232},{"author":"QCRI","authorData":{"_id":"5fbffdf6b9e35d457aa46